    "diagnosis": "Chondroblastic osteosarcoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The principal differential diagnosis for childhood chondrosarcoma is chondroblastic osteosarcoma. The latter may show hyaline cartilage differentiation but in general tends to exhibit a greater degree of atypia relative to the cellularity.",
    "source": "Scott E. Kilpatrick",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/44/226/18928.jpg",
